  <name>Git Desk</name>
  <summary>A native GNOME Git client</summary>
  
  <description>
    <p>
      Git Desk is a powerful yet easy-to-use Git client designed for GNOME.
      It provides a clean, modern interface for managing your Git repositories
      with all the features you need for daily development.
    </p>
    <p>
      Whether you're a beginner learning Git or an experienced developer,
      Git Desk makes version control approachable without hiding how Git works.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Repository management (clone, init, open)</li>
      <li>Commit, push, pull, and more</li>
      <li>Branch and tag management</li>
      <li>Stash support</li>
      <li>Diff viewer with syntax highlighting</li>
      <li>History graph visualization</li>
      <li>Built-in Git Guide for learning</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
  
  <categories>
    <category>Development</category>
    <category>VersionControl</category>
  </categories>
  
